      "content": "it just feels so exhausting. like, i've spent my whole life running a race that just ended in a dead end. there's no \"rebuilding\" when the foundation itself is gone. everything i am is just... hollow. it feels like i'm just staying alive out of habit, but there's nothing left to live for. doesn't it seem kind of illogical to just keep dragging this empty version of myself around indefinitely?",
